  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday night through next Tuesday)\nIssued at 1015 PM CST Tue Nov 24 2026\n\nNot much in the way of impactful weather awaits the final days of\nNovember. The upper pattern transitions from a slower, amplified \nflow to a more progressive and zonal regime by early next week. \nOur winds aloft Thursday night will have swung northwesterly \nthanks to a weak shortwave trough's passage, and this flow \nlingers through Saturday allowing lee troughing and SW breezes to \nboost our high temps. On that note, multiple runs of the ECM and \nits ensembles have been favoring higher downslope winds for \nSaturday compared to the GEFS/GFS due to a more robust shortwave \ntrough descending into the southern Great Plains. Since the NBM \nhas a heavier contribution of the ECM than the GFS in the extended\nrealm, feel its winds are trending the right way despite still \nlagging the 25-35 mph winds of the ECM and its MOS. The shortwave\nsends a cold front our way Saturday night devoid of moisture, so \nother than breezy N winds and cooler highs in the 50s for Sunday \nwe foresee no impacts. Stronger and more zonal flow ensues \nthereafter with milder highs as we turn the page to December.",
